+issueNumber: MDL-89296
+notes:
+  core:
+    - message: >-
+        A new PHP API is available for mounting React components. The
+        `renderer_base::render_react_component()` method (and the lower-level
+        `html_writer::react_component()`) generates a mount point for a React
+        component given only the component specifier and its props. Prop
+        serialisation, escaping, and the DOM contract used by the
+        `core/react_autoinit` system are handled internally.
+      type: improved
+    - message: >-
+        A new `core\output\react_renderable` interface is available. When a
+        renderable implementing it is rendered with `renderer_base::render()`,
+        a React mount point for the component it specifies is generated
+        automatically. It has a higher precedence than `named_templatable` and
+        `templatable`, and a lower precedence than a `render_[renderable]`
+        method in the renderer.
+      type: improved
